i susan parsonage acting returning  officer for the lancaster and fleet word  parliamentary constituency declare that  the total number of votes given to each  candidate was as follows  Robin Eamonn long Liberal Democrats  1117  [Music]  Rebecca joy Novell 796  [Applause]  Eric Halloran Shaw the Conservative  Party candidate 18,000 681  [Applause]  Catherine Jane Smith Labour Party 25,000  [Applause]  I gave public notice that Katherine Jane  Smith is duly elected as the Member of  Parliament for the Lancaster and fleet  word constituency the total number of  votes cast across Lancaster and  Fleetwood at the UK parliamentary  election on 8th of June 2017 was 46,000  and 82 the total number of ballot papers  rejected was 93 the ballot papers were  rejected for the following reasons one  was rejected because it did not bear the  official mark 13 ballot papers were  rejected because votes were given to  more than one candidate for pilot papers  were rejected because there was  something written or marked on the  ballot paper by which the voter could be  identified and 75 ballot papers were  rejected because they were unmarked or  void from certainty congratulations to  you  [Applause]  I'm incredibly grateful to the voters of  Lancaster and Fleetwood who place their  trust in me once more and I hope to  repay the trust in serving as your  Member of Parliament and working hard  entirely for our community results like  this and others across the country show  that voters are increasingly turning  against the failed conservative dogma we  seized cuts to our NHS schools and  public services and which is seen wages  fail to keep up with prices rejected  this racism button which sees the many  pay the price for the perks of the few  the voters in our community and many  others across the country have chosen  the politics of Hope over the politics  of fear and division I would like to  thank the police and the returning  officer and council staff for the  running of this election and the count  I'd like to thank my agent and my  wonderful campaign team and all those  hundreds of people who came out and  volunteered across this constituency I'd  like to thank the voters and everybody  who took part in the democratic process  including the candidates and campaign  team from the other parties to everybody  who takes part in our democracy thank  you
 

